On Aug 23, 2015, at 1:58 PM, Nikki Budzinski <nbudzinski@hillaryclinton.com=
>
wrote:

Hi guys
Ok, some feedback for your consideration regarding the Op Ed and fact
sheet.  Would you be willing to let me know if any of these suggestions you
think are possible?  I'd appreciate knowing where you finally land.  I
think with the trades one of the most important things is to provide them a
heads up, even if we're going to be in different places.  I'd like to be
able to do that when appropriate.

Not surprising I know, but the trades are going to go nuclear (so to speak)
on the Administration once this announcement comes out.  They will likely
attack around the argument that this decision will lead to increased energy
prices for those on fixed incomes.  They will also point out that if his
rationale is increased CO2 exposure, HRC's State Department said there will
negligible traces.  Just a fyi.

1.  Thank you Trevor for breaking it down, that was really helpful.  I do
think the grid piece and the pipeline infrastructure piece will be liked.
2.  Could we include the terminology around "current baseload needs" in the
current energy economy in both the fact sheet and Op Ed?  This will at
least tip the hat to where we are today with the acknowledgement that we
are transitioning to green.
3.  When we talk about infrastructure standards, could we please mention
prevailing wage and project labor agreements as one good set of standards?
4.  Could we beef up the mentioning jobs?  O'Malley made the mistake with
the trades of stating that energy jobs are temporary.  They really bristle
at that.  Could we mention that these are "jobs and careers" for many
workers and as we transition HRC wants to create more careers within the
new energy economy?  Careers is their buzz word.
5.  As I mention above, the Trades will attack Obama on raising energy
prices, could HRC's OpEd and Fact sheet mention that she wants to see
protections for consumers for those potential rising prices?

The Op Ed will be read as very celebratory, and maybe that's it.  But I
think if we could incorporate a little of these suggestions above and tone,
it could be helpful.

I'd love to hear what you think and if anything is possible.  Thank you
again for the heads up.  I appreciate it.

Thanks
Nikki

